          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Keguang Xu",
          "email": "kxu@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-26 03:32:51.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Keguang Xu",
          "email": "kxu@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-26 04:06:47.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20205 ldlm: fix hpreq_check when first cancel lock is gone",
        "message": "LU-20205 ldlm: fix hpreq_check when first cancel lock is gone\n\nWith HPREQ_CHECK1, ldlm_cancel_hpreq_check() only checks the first\nlock handle. But this lock can already be gone on the server, while\nBL_AST locks packed behind it still need the HP queue:\n- the lock was taken for LRU cancel, which clears CANCEL_ON_BLOCK,\n  and then got a BL_AST, so the server already cancelled it;\n- the lock was force-packed by ldlm_cancel_pack() in ldlm_cli_cancel()\n  after another cancel RPC also packed it, and that RPC was handled\n  first.\nIn both cases the check stops at i > 0 and returns 0, so the cancel\nRPC is not HP and the client may be evicted on lock callback timeout.\n\nStop after the first lock only if it still exists. Otherwise scan the\nother locks for AST_SENT as before.\n\nFixes: 4e3fc93dc763 (\"LU-20205 ldlm: no need to check all locks in hpreq_check\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nSigned-off-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Ib6acbc088cfad5044793863f870e548d529b17f3\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
